# Lives at the REPOSITORY ROOT because that is the build context, and because
# every Docker version reads it here. BuildKit would also accept
# freementor/server/Dockerfile.dockerignore, but the classic builder would
# not — and a .dockerignore that is silently skipped bakes .env into a layer.
#
# The first entry is the one that matters: .env holds the Postgres password,
# the Supabase service key and the YouTube key, and a COPY of the server
# directory would otherwise bake all three into a layer. Layers are not
# secret — anybody who can pull the image can read them.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# The app, admin panel and library are not part of the API image.
freementor/app/
freementor/admin/
freementor/shared/
library/
design/
web/
docs/
# ...except the policy pages the API serves.
!docs/legal/

**/node_modules/
**/.expo/
**/dist/
**/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/*.egg-info/

# Local-mode database; can hold real test data and is rebuilt on boot.
**/freementor-local.db

.git/
.github/
**/tests/
**/*.md
!docs/legal/*.md
